<%#
  Controller resolution for a dial-capable action's Property Inspector (#759, #1329).
  One copy for all 17 dial PIs: a host that changes how it reports the controller
  is patched here, not in every template.

  Include it ONCE per dial PI, before the template's own <script>, which calls:

    window.irdResolveController()  -> "Encoder" | "Keypad" | null
    window.irdApplyDialView()      -> hides #keypad-settings and #keypad-appearance,
                                      shows #dial-settings

  The view switch stays in the template, because the order is the template's:
  most resolve last in their initialize(), after wiring the keypad view, so a
  slow or failed lookup still leaves a working keypad PI. A template with more to
  reveal on a dial (Fuel Service's key bindings, Audio Controls' dial-only
  bindings) does it beside its own call, after irdApplyDialView().

  No parameters.
%>
<script>
	(function () {
		// Which surface this instance sits on: the PI registration's
		// actionInfo.payload.controller ("Keypad" | "Encoder"; the Mirabox host
		// reports a knob as "Knob"). A missing controller means a keypad (a host
		// that declares no dials sends none). A failed lookup returns null: the
		// surface is then unknown. A caller that only asks `=== "Encoder"` keeps
		// the keypad view on it; Audio Controls also wires neither surface (#1196).
		window.irdResolveController = async function () {
			try {
				const client = window.SDPIComponents && window.SDPIComponents.streamDeckClient;
				const info = client && (await client.getConnectionInfo());
				const controller = info && info.actionInfo && info.actionInfo.payload && info.actionInfo.payload.controller;
				return controller === "Encoder" || controller === "Knob" ? "Encoder" : "Keypad";
			} catch (err) {
				return null;
			}
		};

		// The dial view: the keypad's own settings and its key-icon appearance go,
		// the dial's settings come. Every dial PI uses these three ids.
		window.irdApplyDialView = function () {
			document.getElementById("keypad-settings")?.classList.add("hidden");
			document.getElementById("keypad-appearance")?.classList.add("hidden");
			document.getElementById("dial-settings")?.classList.remove("hidden");
		};
	})();
</script>
